# <Shania Start>
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
# [DevOps: Secrets management] Real credentials are NEVER committed.
#
# A bare ".env" line was not enough. On 30 July 2026 a file named "..env" reached this
# public repository, because "..env" does not match the pattern ".env" — git compares the
# whole name, and the extra leading dot makes it a different one. The lines below cover
# every shape that name can take, and the negation keeps the one file we do want tracked.
# Prove any change here with: git check-ignore -v '..env'
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example

# Private keys, in every extension we are likely to meet. The EC2 SSH key sits on disk
# while anyone works on deployment, and a public repository is an unforgiving place to
# discover that.
*.pem
*.key
*.ppk
id_rsa
id_ed25519

.DS_Store
# <Shania End>

# <Rebecca Member 2 Start>
public/uploads/*
!public/uploads/.gitkeep
# <Rebecca Member 2 End>
src/data/scamWeatherPosts.json
src/data/scamWeatherArticles.json

